  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Peter",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 1,
    "summary": "Peter urges the Saints to make their calling and election sure—Prophecy comes by the power of the Holy Ghost.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Simon Peter, a servant and an apostle of Jesus Christ, to them that have obtained like precious faith with us through the righteousness of God and our Saviour Jesus Christ:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "TG Servant."
          },
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "D&C 107:23."
          },
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 95,
            "text": "GR equally precious."
          },
          {
            "start": 122,
            "end": 135,
            "text": "TG God, the Standard of Righteousness."
          },
          {
            "start": 136,
            "end": 138,
            "text": "GR of our God and Savior."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Grace and peace be multiplied unto you through the knowledge of God, and of Jesus our Lord,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 60,
            "text": "D&C 76:7 (5–10)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "According as his divine power hath given unto us all things that pertain unto life and godliness, through the knowledge of him that hath called us to glory and virtue:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "D&C 76:55 (53–60)."
          },
          {
            "start": 78,
            "end": 82,
            "text": "D&C 45:8."
          },
          {
            "start": 87,
            "end": 96,
            "text": "TG Godliness."
          },
          {
            "start": 147,
            "end": 149,
            "text": "GR through, by."
          },
          {
            "start": 160,
            "end": 166,
            "text": "TG Virtue."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 72
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Whereby are given unto us exceeding great and precious promises: that by these ye might be partakers of the divine nature, having escaped the corruption that is in the world through lust.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "TG Promise."
          },
          {
            "start": 91,
            "end": 100,
            "text": "D&C 93:28 (27–28)."
          },
          {
            "start": 108,
            "end": 114,
            "text": "TG Earth, Purpose of."
          },
          {
            "start": 115,
            "end": 121,
            "text": "1 Sam. 10:6."
          },
          {
            "start": 130,
            "end": 137,
            "text": "2 Pet. 2:18."
          },
          {
            "start": 142,
            "end": 152,
            "text": "TG Man, Natural, Not Spiritually Reborn."
          },
          {
            "start": 182,
            "end": 186,
            "text": "TG Lust."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And beside this, giving all diligence, add to your faith virtue; and to virtue knowledge;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "TG Diligence."
          },
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 63,
            "text": "TG Chastity; Good Works; Virtue."
          },
          {
            "start": 79,
            "end": 88,
            "text": "TG Knowledge; Learn; Study."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And to knowledge temperance; and to temperance patience; and to patience godliness;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 27,
            "text": "GR self-control. TG Temperance."
          },
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "TG Patience."
          },
          {
            "start": 73,
            "end": 82,
            "text": "GR reverence, piety, godliness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And to godliness brotherly kindness; and to brotherly kindness charity.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "TG Brotherhood and Sisterhood."
          },
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "TG Benevolence; Kindness."
          },
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 70,
            "text": "TG Charity."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For if these things be in you, and abound, they make you that ye shall neither be barren nor unfruitful in the knowledge of our Lord Jesus Christ.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 41,
            "text": "TG Abundant Life."
          },
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 88,
            "text": "GR idle, unprofitable, injurious. TG Barren."
          },
          {
            "start": 93,
            "end": 103,
            "text": "D&C 107:31 (30–31)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 70
          },
          {
            "start": 79,
            "end": 81
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But he that lacketh these things is blind, and cannot see afar off, and hath forgotten that he was purged from his old sins.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Wherefore the rather, brethren, give diligence to make your calling and election sure: for if ye do these things, ye shall never fall:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 80,
            "text": "TG Election."
          },
          {
            "start": 129,
            "end": 133,
            "text": "D&C 50:44."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For so an entrance shall be ministered unto you abundantly into the everlasting kingdom of our Lord and Saviour Jesus Christ.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 79,
            "text": "TG Immortality."
          },
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 87,
            "text": "TG Kingdom of God, on Earth."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Wherefore I will not be negligent to put you always in remembrance of these things, though ye know them, and be established in the present truth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 99,
            "end": 104
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Yea, I think it meet, as long as I am in this tabernacle, to stir you up by putting you in remembrance;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "GR right, just, righteous."
          },
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 56,
            "text": "D&C 93:4, 35."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 87
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Knowing that shortly I must put off this my tabernacle, even as our Lord Jesus Christ hath shewed me.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 91,
            "end": 97,
            "text": "John 21:19 (18–19)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 40
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Moreover I will endeavour that ye may be able after my decease to have these things always in remembrance.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For we have not followed cunningly devised fables, when we made known unto you the power and coming of our Lord Jesus Christ, but were eyewitnesses of his majesty.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 49,
            "text": "1 Tim. 1:4."
          },
          {
            "start": 135,
            "end": 147,
            "text": "Matt. 17:2 (1–9); John 1:14. TG Witness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For he received from God the Father honour and glory, when there came such a voice to him from the excellent glory, This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 127,
            "end": 138,
            "text": "TG Witness of the Father."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And this voice which came from heaven we heard, when we were with him in the holy mount.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "TG Revelation; Witness of the Father."
          },
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 87,
            "text": "Luke 9:28 (28–36)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "We have also a more sure word of prophecy; whereunto ye do well that ye take heed, as unto a light that shineth in a dark place, until the day dawn, and the day star arise in your hearts:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 2,
            "text": "JST 2 Pet. 1:19 We have therefore a more sure knowledge of the word of prophecy, to which word of prophecy ye do well that ye take heed …"
          },
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "D&C 68:12; 88:3 (3–4); 132:19, 49."
          },
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 41,
            "text": "D&C 131:5."
          },
          {
            "start": 161,
            "end": 165,
            "text": "Rev. 2:28; 22:16 (6–16)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Knowing this first, that no prophecy of the scripture is of any private interpretation.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 27,
            "text": "JST 2 Pet. 1:20 … no prophecy of the scriptures is given of any private will of man."
          },
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 36,
            "text": "TG Prophecy."
          },
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 53,
            "text": "TG Scriptures, Study of."
          },
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 86,
            "text": "Gen. 40:8."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For the prophecy came not in old time by the will of man: but holy men of God spake as they were moved by the Holy Ghost.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "TG Prophecy; Scriptures, Value of; Scriptures, Writing of."
          },
          {
            "start": 78,
            "end": 83,
            "text": "TG Holy Ghost, Mission of."
          },
          {
            "start": 97,
            "end": 102,
            "text": "TG Inspiration."
          },
          {
            "start": 110,
            "end": 120,
            "text": "TG Holy Ghost, Gifts of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 96
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
